# Settings for us-bins-2026-08-22.csv.
#
# Trusted BELOW binlist-data.csv, which sits at 0.5. binlist-data.csv is the
# reference: where the two name a different bank for the same BIN, the
# reference is what the tool answers with and this file is set aside.
#
# That is the list owner's call, not something the files settle between them.
# Both readings stay on record either way — the losing one is kept as recorded
# dissent, and `python -m app.cli origin <bin>` prints each source row as it
# arrived. To reverse it, put this above 0.5.
#
# A blank is not a clash. Where the reference says nothing about a BIN's bank,
# card level or card type, this file still fills it in, and the 9 BINs the
# reference does not hold at all still come in from here.
#
# The `notes` column carries the LEVEL and BANK columns exactly as the source
# printed them, before they were split apart. The reader never ingests it, so
# it costs nothing and every split stays checkable against what was read.
# bintel: confidence = 0.4
